{
 "esm": "1.1.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "EqWeatherScm",
  "description": "EqWeather-SCM: the STATE document of PLAN.md 3.1 -- the dynamics half (couplings/eqweather_scm_dynamics.esm) and the physics half (couplings/scm_physics_column.esm) CO-MOUNTED over one shared ODE state, which is what neither half could be on its own. Ten states are integrated here: the five WRF-ARW prognostics u, v, w, phi' and theta_m, the three moist species q_v, q_c and q_i, the soil column T_s and the skin temperature T_sk. Every tendency is a SUM, and forming those sums is the whole point of the document: D(u) and D(v) take the perturbation-Coriolis, curvature and sponge tendencies plus YSU's RUBLTEN/RVBLTEN; D(theta_m) takes the sponge plus WRFMoistThetaTendency's conversion of the radiative and PBL theta and q_v tendencies; D(q_v), D(q_c) and D(q_i) are YSU's RQVBLTEN/RQCBLTEN/RQIBLTEN; D(T_s) and D(T_sk) are the slab's. The state goes back into all sixteen mounted components through document-level coupling.variable_map param_to_var edges, so nothing about the column is read from a dump that the state could supply: WRFColumnGeometry recomputes the heights, the equation of state, the Exner function, the layer temperature and the hydrostatic interface pressure from theta_m, q_v and phi' at every right-hand-side evaluation, and those feed YSU, Dudhia SW, the RRTM longwave chain and cal_cldfra; the surface layer and the slab read the lowest layer by indexing the state and the geometry rather than a prescribed u1/t1/p1/dz1; and the skin temperature the radiation emits from is the same ODE state the surface layer exchanges with and the slab integrates. cal_cldfra closes the last of those edges: the grid-scale cloud fraction the longwave sees is COMPUTED here from the state (components/atmospheric_radiation/cloud_fraction/cal_cldfra.esm, WRF's cal_cldfra1 at icloud = 1) instead of being prescribed from the dumped CLDFRA of the reference call, which is what every frozen-column document in couplings/ had to do. KNOWN LIMITS, all of them absences rather than approximations, and all exact at t = 0: (a) NO MICROPHYSICS is mounted, so q_r, q_s and q_g are held at their step-1410 profiles (read by reference from the same hand-authored libraries the frozen-column documents use) and q_c and q_i only diffuse; (b) the column mass mu' is constant, as in the dynamics half -- a horizontally uniform periodic column has no mass-flux divergence; (c) the total water q_t entering the hydrostatic interface pressure is the step-1410 profile rather than the sum of the evolving species, so p_hyd carries an O(dq_v mu_d) staleness that is zero at t = 0; (d) psfc is prescribed, because WRF carries it rather than rediagnosing it; (e) there is no acoustic sub-step or off-centring, so the undamped vertical acoustic mode of the dynamics half is present here too (see that document's own 60 s test for its measured amplitude). WHAT IS ASSERTED, and why there is no trajectory test: ONE right-hand-side evaluation of this document costs 1 h 47 m of wall clock, measured -- against 86 s for the nine-component physics column, and with nothing integrated and no Jacobian formed (the test's time span is empty). A 24 h run is therefore out of reach at the cost measured on EarthSciAST main at 3cf6f6f92. That cost is an interpreter defect rather than a property of this model: EarthSciAST #438, fixed in PR #439 -- the Rust driver built an implicit solver even for a run that cannot advance, and materialising its finite-difference Jacobian costs 2*n_states + 1 full right-hand-side evaluations to return the untouched initial state. With that fixed the same 65/65 takes 2 m 31 s. RE-TIME THIS DOCUMENT, AND THE ACCEPTANCE QUESTION OF PLAN.md 3.1, WHEN #439 LANDS; the test's own description records the measurements and the hypotheses they ruled out. What this document therefore pins is that the loop CLOSES and that closing it changes nothing: at t = 0, with the state set to the WRF step-1410 column, every tendency and every diagnostic still meets the same references the two halves assert separately, and the cloud fraction the longwave sees is computed here rather than prescribed.",
  "license": "MIT",
  "tags": [
   "wrf",
   "coupling",
   "single-column",
   "state-document",
   "eqweather"
  ]
 },
 "metaparameters": {
  "NLEV": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 59,
   "description": "Number of model layers (WRF kte), bound into every mount edge so all column schemes resolve their grid at the same size; 59 is the em_scm_xy reference column. The leaves' own index sets merge into this document's registry at the mount edge (esm-spec 4.7), so the document declares no index_sets of its own."
  },
  "NBUF": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 44,
   "description": "Number of buffer layers MM5ATM adds above the model top, nint(p_top / (100 deltap)) with deltap = 4 hPa (RRTMINIT: NLAYERS = kme + nint(p_top*0.01/deltap) - 1); 44 for the reference column (p_top = 177.6 hPa). Bound into each RRTM mount edge."
  },
  "NGPT": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 140,
   "description": "Declared at document level because the mounted leaves' index sets are redeclared here (a top-level ref mount does not merge the leaf's index_sets; EarthSciAST issue #198) and bound into every mount edge. Number of g-points after the 256-to-140 reduction."
  },
  "NBANDS": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 16,
   "description": "Declared at document level because the mounted leaves' index sets are redeclared here (a top-level ref mount does not merge the leaf's index_sets; EarthSciAST issue #198) and bound into every mount edge. Number of longwave bands."
  },
  "PLANCK_T0": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 159,
   "description": "Declared at document level because the mounted leaves' index sets are redeclared here (a top-level ref mount does not merge the leaf's index_sets; EarthSciAST issue #198) and bound into every mount edge. TOTPLNK(i, band) holds the band Planck integral at T = PLANCK_T0 + i kelvin, i = 1..181 (RRTM's INDLEV = INT(T - 159.))."
  },
  "PLANCK_NODES": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 181,
   "description": "Declared at document level because the mounted leaves' index sets are redeclared here (a top-level ref mount does not merge the leaf's index_sets; EarthSciAST issue #198) and bound into every mount edge. Temperature nodes of the TOTPLNK table (160..340 K)."
  },
  "NSOIL": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 4,
   "description": "Number of PROGNOSTIC soil layers of the mounted slab (WRF num_soil_layers - 1 = 4; the deepest WRF layer is the fixed reservoir T_deep). Bound into the Lsm mount edge, whose column axis is renamed soil/soil_nodes so it does not collide with the 59-layer atmospheric lev (esm-spec 4.7 mount-edge index_set_rename, EarthSciAST #213)."
  }
 },
