    {
     "id": "eqweather_scm_step1410",
     "description": "The two halves of EqWeather-SCM on ONE shared state, at the state of WRF step 1410 (radiation call 2820): 18:29 UTC, 12:02 local solar time, the strongest daytime forcing of the 24 h em_scm_xy reference run. The initial condition is that step's column -- u, v, w, phi', theta_m and q_v from the dynamics half's own step-1410 test, q_c and q_i from couplings/tests/physics_step1410_atmos_inputs.esm, the four soil layers from scm_step1410_soil_inputs.esm and the skin temperature from the physics half's tsk -- so at t = 0 the coupled column IS the reference column and every reference below is the one the two halves already assert separately. TIME SPAN {0, 0} is the instantaneous-derivative shape of esm-spec 6.6.2, not a shortened run: with an empty interval the run's whole answer is its initial state and nothing is integrated to reach it, which is exactly what a test of tendencies asserted at t = 0 wants. WHAT IS ASSERTED. The 9 dynamics assertions are couplings/eqweather_scm_dynamics.esm's, at its tolerances, with du_dt, dv_dt and dtheta_m_dt renamed to the *_dyn parts because those three names now carry the SUM. The 52 physics assertions are couplings/scm_physics_column.esm's, unchanged, at its tolerances. Running them here is not a repetition: in this document nothing about the column is read from a dump that the state could supply. WRFColumnGeometry rebuilds the heights, the equation of state, the Exner function, the layer temperature and the hydrostatic interface pressure from theta_m, q_v and phi' and hands them to YSU, Dudhia SW, the RRTM chain and cal_cldfra; u1, v1 and qv1 are indexed out of the ODE state and t1, p1 and dz1 out of the geometry, where the frozen-column documents prescribed all six; and the skin temperature is an ODE state that the surface layer, the longwave surface emission and the slab's energy balance all read, where it was a constant before. Every one of those paths is a place the assembly could have disagreed with WRF and does not. FOUR ASSERTIONS ARE NEW and cannot exist in either half. du_dt, dv_dt and dtheta_m_dt are compared against the SUM of the two halves' own references -- the sums this document was built to form, and the only place a dropped, doubled or sign-flipped term would show. PLAN.md 3.1 measured the dynamics D(theta_m) at 1.02e-5 K/s against the physics half's 3.80e-4, so that third one is dominated by the physics and pins that the small term was added rather than lost. The fourth is cldfra: cal_cldfra computing, from this document's own state, the one radiation input every frozen-column document in couplings/ had to prescribe, against the CLDFRA the same WRF call handed RRTM. MEASURED, whole assembly, 47 + 18 -> 65/65. Fourteen surface-layer assertions and pbl_hpbl take the GEOMETRY tolerances rather than the physics suite's, for a reason already isolated in this repo: t1, p1 and dz1 now come from WRFColumnGeometry, whose lowest-layer pressure sits 0.30 Pa below the p1 the surface-layer kernel was dumped with (N50, the driver-versus-kernel offset), which moves the surface-air theta by about 8e-5 relative. Residuals: sfc_hfx 7.3e-5, sfc_mol 7.1e-5, sfc_br 4.8e-5, sfc_rmol 4.7e-5, sfc_psim 2.3e-5, sfc_psih 2.0e-5, sfc_flhc 9.2e-6, sfc_fh 7.0e-6, sfc_qfx 5.2e-6, sfc_lh 5.2e-6, sfc_flqc 5.2e-6, sfc_fm 4.2e-6, sfc_ust 2.1e-6, sfc_q2 1.8e-6 relative -- the SAME fourteen numbers, to two significant figures, that couplings/geometry_surface_pbl_column.esm measured for that substitution ALONE. That agreement is the result: co-mounting the two halves introduced nothing of its own. pbl_hpbl, at 5.1e-6, is the one not on that list, because radiation IS mounted here and YSU sees a computed rthraten instead of a prescribed one. Everything else meets the two halves' own tolerances unchanged: all twelve PBL and slab tendency assertions, the longwave fluxes and heating, gsw/glw/olr, and the nine dynamics assertions including p_p and dphi_dt = g w at 1e-12. THE THREE SUMS come out at Linf 6.2e-5 (du_dt), 3.0e-5 (dv_dt) and 1.1e-4 K/s (dtheta_m_dt), each well inside the tolerance its own PBL part already carries (5e-4, 2e-4, 1e-3), so the terms are added and none is doubled or dropped; tolerances are 3x measured. CLDFRA matches WRF's exactly, at abs 0 -- but note what that does and does not show: step 1410 is a clear column (three layers of trace cirrus, q_i <= 2.1e-9, all below cal_cldfra1's 0.01 snap), so both are identically zero and the assertion pins the WIRING and the zero, not the fractional fit. cal_cldfra's own six-regime test set is where the fit, the phase blend and the floors are exercised. COST, measured. Against EarthSciAST main at 3cf6f6f92 this test is 110 m 36 s of wall clock for ONE right-hand-side evaluation; against the fix in EarthSciAST PR #439 it is 2 m 31 s, with the same 65/65. THE CAUSE IS NOT THIS MODEL, and it is not what the first diagnosis of it said. The Rust driver built a diffsol problem and an implicit solver for EVERY run, including one that cannot advance -- an empty time span, or a non-empty one whose whole output grid sits at t0. Constructing an implicit solver materialises the Jacobian, and this crate's is a matrix-free finite-difference JVP, so it is called once per state column and each call evaluates the entire right-hand side twice: 2*n_states + 1 full evaluations to return a trajectory that is the untouched initial state. With 297 states, each re-materialising the whole RRTM longwave chain, that is the hour and three quarters. WHAT COSTS IS THE STATE COUNT -- not the recurrence in rtrn_sweep and not the geometry path. Measured three ways on the reproducers under data/eqwefic/phase3_probes/: a 103-deep self-referential sweep with NO state runs in 0.03 s; the SAME sweep with ONE scalar state that it DEPENDS ON runs in 0.09 s; the same sweep over 103 states runs in 1.84 s. Two further hypotheses were ruled out before that: it is not the param_to_var edge or a const-node-versus-parameter distinction (routing the same five dumped columns into the radiation mount through document variables and coupling edges costs 19.27 -> 19.85 s, nothing), and it is not ODE states as such in a CHEAP document (an unused scalar D(s) = 0 leaves the static radiation column at 19.06 s) -- what multiplies is the state count times the cost of one evaluation. BDF over a 1 s span, tried before the empty span, had not finished a single step in 14 minutes, which is the same Jacobian plus real stepping. RE-TIME THIS DOCUMENT WHEN #439 LANDS, and re-time the whole repository with it: the same defect was charging every test written in the standard {start: 0, end: 1} shape with assertions only at t = 0.",
